    "body": "**TLDR:** By default the validation console line never shows the validation reward, because it looks up `validation/reward/_mean` but the key is `validation_reward/_mean`. This PR renames the two default patterns.\n\n**Problem**\n1. `compute_rollout_metrics(prefix=\"validation\")` logs the reward as `validation_reward`, with sub-keys `validation_reward/_mean`, `validation_reward/_max` and so on.\n2. `MetricsProcessor.Config.console_log_keys_validation` defaults to `validation/reward/_mean` and `validation/reward/_max`, which match no key.\n3. Recipes that keep the default (alphabet_sort, search_r1) print no reward on the validation console line. The recipes that set their own list already use `validation_reward/_mean`.\n\n**Solution**\n1. Rename the two default patterns to `validation_reward/_mean` and `validation_reward/_max`.\n2. The other defaults (`validation/response_length/mean`, `timing/validate`) already match their keys and don't change.\n\n**Results**\n`MetricsProcessor.log(is_validation=True)` on `compute_rollout_metrics` output for 2 rollouts with rewards 1 and 0:\n```\nbefore: Validation | Step:  0  timing/validate: 1.50\nafter:  Validation | Step:  0  validation_reward/_mean: 0.50  validation_reward/_max: 1.0  timing/validate: 1.50\n```\n\n**Test plan**\n- `pytest tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_metrics.py`: 81 passed.\n- The console check above.\n- `pre-commit run` on the changed file.\n\n",
